 641:Core/Src/main.c **** #define ADC_VREF              3.3f
 642:Core/Src/main.c **** #define ADC_FULL_SCALE_CODES  2048.0f  // ADC1 is differential; signed code -2048..2047 spans -VREF
 643:Core/Src/main.c **** #define V_PEAK_NOM            200.0f
 644:Core/Src/main.c **** 
 645:Core/Src/main.c **** /**
 646:Core/Src/main.c ****  * Sensor transfer function (measured/derived from the actual circuit):
 647:Core/Src/main.c ****  *   Vout_p = Vin * (250/22000) *  0.43 + 1.65V
 648:Core/Src/main.c ****  *   Vout_n = Vin * (250/22000) * -0.43 + 1.65V
 649:Core/Src/main.c ****  * Both differential pins are biased at 1.65V (VDDA/2) with the signal
 650:Core/Src/main.c ****  * riding symmetrically in opposite directions, so the differential the ADC
 651:Core/Src/main.c ****  * actually measures is:
 652:Core/Src/main.c ****  *   Vinp - Vinn = Vout_p - Vout_n = SENSOR_GAIN * Vin
 653:Core/Src/main.c ****  * where SENSOR_GAIN = 2 * (250/22000) * 0.43. The 1.65V bias on each pin
 654:Core/Src/main.c ****  * cancels out in the subtraction -- no bias removal needed in software.
